# The image only needs python/ + requirements.txt; everything below is dev-
# machine state that has no business being copied into the build context.
# Without this, `COPY . .` was pulling in the local .venv (8.2GB on EC2,
# includes a full CUDA torch install) and data/ (3GB of raw images + eval
# results), which blew past the EC2 root volume's free space mid-build.
.venv
.git
.github
.docs
data
docs
__pycache__
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
.env.bak.*
*.pem
*.bundle
